<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE presentation SYSTEM "https://corepunch.github.io/presenter/schemas/presentation.dtd">
<presentation name="Theme Studio" style="./styles/Studio.style">
  <slide title="Beautiful slides.">
    <notes>Presenter pairs a polished deck with private speaker notes. Let your agent organize the source material and write a natural script, then review the result before your meeting.</notes>
    <stack margin="60" gap="24" verticalAlignment="center">
      <text role="title">Beautiful slides.</text>
      <text role="subtitle" color="muted">Words to say.</text>
    </stack>
  </slide>
  <slide title="Ready for the room.">
    <notes>The audience sees your slides. Your speaking notes stay in a separate window. Share only the audience window in your meeting app.</notes>
    <grid rows="auto *" gap="24" margin="40">
      <text role="heading">Ready for the room.</text>
      <grid row="1" columns="* *" rows="*" gap="24">
        <grid rows="auto *" gap="24" row="0" column="0">
          <text role="heading">A clear story</text>
          <stack row="1" gap="20">
            <icon name="layer-group">Stacks and grids</icon>
            <icon name="palette">Coordinated themes</icon>
            <icon name="chart-bar">Charts from your data</icon>
          </stack>
        </grid>
        <grid rows="auto *" gap="24" row="0" column="1">
          <text role="heading">A confident delivery</text>
          <stack row="1" gap="20">
            <icon name="comment">Private speaker notes</icon>
            <icon name="desktop">Separate audience window</icon>
            <icon name="folder">Portable slide packages</icon>
          </stack>
        </grid>
      </grid>
    </grid>
  </slide>
  <slide title="Make the numbers legible.">
    <notes>This chart uses illustrative data to demonstrate the theme palette. These values are not product measurements.</notes>
    <grid rows="auto *" gap="24" margin="40">
      <text role="heading">Make the numbers legible.</text>
      <stack row="1" gap="20">
        <chart type="bar" title="Illustrative project milestones">
          <point label="Discover" value="24" />
          <point label="Design" value="48" />
          <point label="Build" value="72" />
          <point label="Launch" value="92" />
        </chart>
      </stack>
    </grid>
  </slide>
  <slide title="A format your agent can read.">
    <notes>The XML package holds slides, notes and relative paths to assets. The code panel uses JetBrains Mono and a syntax palette coordinated with the theme.</notes>
    <grid rows="auto *" gap="24" margin="40">
      <text role="heading">A format your agent can read.</text>
      <stack row="1" gap="20">
        <code lang="xml">&lt;slide title="Your next idea"&gt;
  &lt;stack margin="60" gap="24"&gt;
    &lt;text role="title"&gt;Your next idea&lt;/text&gt;
    &lt;text&gt;Ready to share.&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;/stack&gt;
&lt;/slide&gt;</code>
      </stack>
    </grid>
  </slide>
  <slide title="Space you can reason about.">
    <notes>The heading spans both columns. The left column receives twice the remaining width of the right. Cards have explicit padding; the footer is measured from its text. No content is automatically scaled.</notes>
    <grid margin="40" columns="2* *" rows="auto * auto" gap="24">
      <text columnSpan="2" role="heading">Space you can reason about.</text>
      <border row="1" padding="28" background="panel" borderColor="line" cornerRadius="20">
        <stack gap="20" verticalAlignment="center">
          <text role="heading" color="accent">Two shares of the space</text>
          <text>Grid allocates widths first. Text then wraps at its actual column width.</text>
          <text role="small" color="muted">Padding: 28 px · Gap: 24 px</text>
        </stack>
      </border>
      <border row="1" column="1" padding="24" background="panel" cornerRadius="20">
        <stack gap="20" verticalAlignment="center">
          <text role="heading">One share</text>
          <text>Short, focused supporting detail.</text>
        </stack>
      </border>
      <stack row="2" columnSpan="2" orientation="horizontal" gap="24">
        <text role="small" color="accent">MEASURE</text>
        <text role="small" color="muted">→</text>
        <text role="small" color="accent">ARRANGE</text>
        <text role="small" color="muted">→</text>
        <text role="small" color="accent">RENDER</text>
      </stack>
    </grid>
  </slide>
</presentation>
